 be verified, restored quickly, and protected from the same threats that endanger the primary data.\n\nHere is a detailed guide on designing a reliable file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Backup Strategies: Full vs. Incremental\nA hybrid approach is generally the most efficient and reliable.\n\n#### Full Backups\nA full backup copies every selected file and folder, regardless of whether they have changed.\n*   **Pros:** Simplest to restore", "elapsed_s": 3.826466217986308, "ttft_s": 0.6872998580220155, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 54, "total_tokens": 182, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 54, "prompt_ms": 485.75800000000004, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.99551851851852, "prompt_per_second": 111.16646560633072, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3139.094, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.717275590551182, "predicted_per_second": 40.45753328826725}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 40.45660071403307, "end_to_end_output_tps": 33.45122959620965, "full_output_budget": true}, "measured": [{"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be restored quickly and accurately when a disaster occurs.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Core Strategy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore diving into technical details, adhere to the industry standard **3-2-1 Backup Rule**:\n*   **3** copies of your data (the original and two backups).\n*   **2** different media types (e.g.,", "elapsed_s": 3.785669865028467, "ttft_s": 0.641260678996332, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 183, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 55, "prompt_ms": 486.214, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.840254545454545, "prompt_per_second": 113.11891471656513, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3144.469, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.759598425196852, "predicted_per_second": 40.388377179104005}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 40.38914545986894, "end_to_end_output_tps": 33.81171749350032, "full_output_budget": true}, {"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be restored quickly and accurately when a disaster occurs.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Foundation: The 3-2-1 Backup Rule\nBefore diving into technical details, adhere to the industry standard **3-2-1 Rule**:\n*   **3** copies of your data (the original and two backups).\n*   **2** different media types (e.g., an", "elapsed_s": 3.729440263006836, "ttft_s": 0.5922045710030943, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 183, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 55, "prompt_ms": 472.943, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.598963636363637, "prompt_per_second": 116.29308394457684, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3137.189, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.70227559055118, "predicted_per_second": 40.48210037712105}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 40.48149787524747, "end_to_end_output_tps": 34.32150429373036, "full_output_budget": true}, {"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be verified, restored quickly, and protected from the same threats that destroyed the original data.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Foundational Strategy: The 3-2-1 Rule\nBefore choosing tools, adhere to the industry standard for data redundancy:\n*   **3 Copies of Data:** Your original data plus two backups.\n*   **2 Different Media Types:** (e.g", "elapsed_s": 3.6778645560261793, "ttft_s": 0.5420836090343073, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 128, "prompt_tokens": 55, "total_tokens": 183, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 55, "prompt_ms": 468.24, "prompt_per_token_ms": 8.513454545454545, "prompt_per_second": 117.4611310439091, "predicted_n": 128, "predicted_ms": 3135.784, "predicted_per_token_ms": 24.6912125984252, "predicted_per_second": 40.500238536838}, "finish_reason": "length", "decode_tps_client": 40.500277968022615, "end_to_end_output_tps": 34.80280419524206, "full_output_budget": true}], "decode_tps_client_median": 40.48149787524747, "ttft_s_median": 0.5922045710030943, "pass": true, "distinct_output_texts": 3}, "long": {"tier": "development", "anchor": {"text": "BOLT-7319-CEDAR", "elapsed_s": 10.791479771025479, "ttft_s": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 11, "prompt_tokens": 8238, "total_tokens": 8249, "prompt_tokens_details": {"cached_tokens": 0}}, "timings": {"cache_n": 0, "prompt_n": 8238, "prompt_ms": 10468.725, "prompt_per_token_ms": 1.2707847778587036, "prompt_per_second": 786.915312036566, "predicted_n": 11, "predicted_ms": 256.492, "predicted_per_token_ms": 25.6492, "predicted_per_second": 38.98757076244093}, "finish_reason": "stop", "decode_tps_client": null, "end_to_end_output_tps": 1.019322672460026, "full_output_budget": false}, "warmup": {"text": "Designing a reliable file backup system requires a shift in mindset from simply \"copying files\" to implementing a **data resilience strategy**. The goal is not just to have a copy of your data, but to ensure that you can recover that data quickly and completely regardless of the failure scenario (hardware crash, ransomware, or natural disaster).\n\nHere is a comprehensive guide to designing a reliable file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Foundation: The 3-2-1 Backup Rule\nBefore diving